1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,240
I think my dad left because he couldn't bear everyone in town thinking he was a thief.

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:10,740
And mom, I bet her not believing him either was really what bothered him the most.

3
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:14,360
The whole thing made me want to stop trusting people.

4
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:17,080
I felt like I was being forced to choose sides.

5
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:20,860
I thought if I hated my mom or my dad, maybe I'd feel better.

6
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:23,580
Then a few years later, I heard my mom say,

7
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,740
why couldn't I just believe him?

8
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:27,900
And I knew she was miserable too.

9
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:34,440
And then, when I heard her say that, I decided to keep on trusting and loving them both.

10
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:41,320
I realized that if there's one thing I'm really good at, it's believing in people.

11
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,900
途切れない明日も過ぎたって

12
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,140
立ち止まって 振り返って

13
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:07,140
止めどない今日を嘆きあった

14
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:10,320
記憶だって 永遠にだって

15
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,320
残らないもんと思い知って

16
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:16,520
僕はずっとかきむしって

17
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:18,960
心の隅っこで泣いた

18
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:22,640
そしてどうかなくさないだよって

19
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:25,700
後悔した過ぎる日々を

20
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:28,840
後悔してんだよって

21
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:30,700
そう言い逃した

22
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,080
もう君

23
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:33,580
君を待った

24
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:35,080
僕は待った

25
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:38,080
途切れない明日も過ぎてって

26
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,820
僕は今日も

27
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,320
かきむしって

28
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:45,320
忘れない傷をつけてるんだよ

29
00:01:45,320 --> 00:02:15,060
最後世界は

30
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:15,260
僕は

31
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,560
What the hell?

32
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,480
I just saw Iri go inside.

33
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:21,120
Then she might be stuck and can't get out.

34
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:22,280
Hey!

35
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,440
Iri!

36
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,440
Iri! Can you hear me?

37
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,000
Iri!

38
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:38,440
Iri!

39
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,120
We gotta go.

40
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:50,540
She's heavy.

41
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:59,600
Hang on. I'll get you out of here.

42
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:03,020
Crap.

43
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,740
I can't lug her down by myself.

44
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:09,320
What are you doing?

45
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,040
You manga guys really should hit the gym more often.

46
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:14,400
Let's hurry before we get barbecued.

47
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:22,900
Get going out the back.

48
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,420
I got her from here.

49
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,800
Don't get her mixed up in your shit.

50
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,580
Guess I get to be the hero today.

51
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:46,200
I hope Iri's okay.

52
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,020
How'd that fire start?

53
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,800
Was it an accident or...

54
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,160
The killer?

55
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:53,920
Wait.

56
00:03:53,920 --> 00:04:00,040
He was trying to kill Iri with that fire.

57
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,320
And he was trying to frame me for it.

58
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,480
That's why she gave me her phone.

59
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:06,320
So the cops wouldn't find the email.

60
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:08,940
He knew where she lived.

61
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,560
Maybe he followed her or...

62
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,960
Maybe she knows him.

63
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:16,700
Whoever he is, he's close.

64
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:19,080
I'm going to find him.

65
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:22,700
And with any luck, I'll get to him before the cops catch me.

66
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:26,440
This is John Koiro.

67
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:28,860
Make sure you hold your belongings before dis...

68
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:30,160
Hello?

69
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,400
Hello?

70
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,000
All right.

71
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:38,720
Who is this?

72
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,100
Satoru Fujinuma.

73
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:46,060
If you're who you say you are, then nice to meet you.

74
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,200
I've been expecting your call.

75
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,840
Sure, be glad to.

76
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:51,920
But not here.

77
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,520
Someplace public.

78
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:57,880
No, I'm not telling you who I am just yet.

79
00:04:58,340 --> 00:04:59,740
Tomorrow, when we meet.

80
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,500
Because if you're not who you say you are,

81
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,740
then you're the son of a bitch that killed Sachko.

82
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:09,420
Sit down anywhere.

83
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:11,400
Oh.

84
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:12,620
Hey, Satoru.

85
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:13,880
Over here.

86
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,540
I'm Sawada.

87
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:18,240
I used to work with your mom at Ishikari TV.

88
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:19,620
God damn.

89
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,460
You look just like Sachko.

90
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:22,480
Yeah.

91
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,540
You're her kid.

92
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:24,480
No doubt about it.

93
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,080
It's him.

94
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,180
I bet you're wondering if you can trust me.

95
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,060
But there's nothing to worry about.

96
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:33,680
I didn't tell the cops you called,

97
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:34,840
and I didn't kill your mom.

98
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:37,480
Yeah, well, maybe you think I killed her.

99
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:38,560
Not even.

100
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:39,780
How can you be sure?

101
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:43,020
Because I knew your mom,

102
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:45,680
and I know she didn't raise the kind of son who'd kill her.

103
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,020
Hmm, I see.

104
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:51,160
Yeah, I remembered I had it in my pocket yesterday.

105
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,060
You're in it deep, that's for sure.

106
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,220
Tell me about it.

107
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,740
And now I'm on the run because I panicked.

108
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,560
I can't stop screwing things up.

109
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:04,380
What happened, happened, so it's pointless to beat yourself up about it.

110
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:04,720
Huh?

111
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:07,760
That's something your mom liked to say.

112
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,760
It's kind of appropriate, don't you think?

113
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,860
You want me to tell you what we talked about the other day?

114
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:17,140
Yeah.

115
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:23,440
Do you remember 18 years ago, when that serial killer was targeting kids?

116
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:24,560
Yeah, sure.

117
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:28,220
Jun Shiratori's still sitting on death row and still denying he killed him.

118
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,880
Well, Satoru was right about him.

119
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:31,480
Huh?

120
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,360
Shiratori's innocent.

121
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:36,360
And I think I figured out who the real killer is.

122
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,800
Can you meet me at Koiwa Station tomorrow?

123
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:42,320
I should have asked for the guy's name.

124
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:49,680
Anyway, let's talk about what happened back then.

125
00:06:49,980 --> 00:06:51,860
About how Kayo Hinazuki died.

126
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,580
We know that on the night of March the 2nd,

127
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:58,740
Kayo's mom and her boyfriend beat her and locked her in the shed.

128
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,980
That was around 10, and she was still alive.

129
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,980
We know she froze to death.

130
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:06,540
And we also know that when the mom and the boyfriend found her body the next morning,

131
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:09,300
they hid it, because they didn't want to take the fall for the murder.

132
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:11,200
But I'm getting ahead of myself.

133
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:15,700
The theory goes that Kayo was taken from the shed sometime after 10 p.m.

134
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:20,040
At about 12.30, Kayo's mom went out to get her and found her gone.

135
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:24,120
Then she called your house and asked your mom if she knew where Kayo was.

136
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,920
When they arrested Jun Shiratori,

137
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:32,120
the only evidence they had that tied him to the crime was a pair of rubber boots he owned.

138
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:34,840
The tread matched tracks they found near the shed.

139
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:39,280
Here's how the police figured the killing went down.

140
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,020
First, he knocked her out and took some pictures of her.

141
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:47,940
Next, he put her in the walk-in freezer at work and sprayed her with water.

142
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:51,540
As soon as her temperature dropped to 20 degrees, she was brain dead.

143
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:56,060
He waited around for about 30 minutes to make sure she was gone.

144
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:00,440
Then, just before dawn, he put her body back in the shed.

145
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:08,080
There's no way Yuki killed her.

146
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:12,240
Kayo Hinazuki, Hiromi Sugita, and Aya Nakanishi.

147
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,320
Just before those three went missing,

148
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:17,620
the same exact thing happened in the next town over from yours.

149
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,860
Someone was quickly arrested,

150
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:22,880
but he swore he was innocent, same as Shiratori.

151
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:24,280
You see?

152
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:26,720
Same crime, same pattern.

153
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,940
It's beyond coincidental.

154
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:31,620
That means...

155
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:32,120
Exactly.

156
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:34,320
I've been trying to tell people for years.

157
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:37,240
They called me crazy, but in the end I was right.

158
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:40,020
These crimes were never really solved.

159
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,340
The killer framed every suspect.

160
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:45,800
So whoever murdered Kayo also murdered Sachiko.

161
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,020
He's still on the loose.

162
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,340
In this city?

163
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,580
This bastard's beyond clever.

164
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:54,620
He plants a false trail of evidence at the scene of the crime

165
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:56,500
that leads the cops away from him

166
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,520
and straight towards some other poor sucker.

167
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,800
And while everyone looks the other way,

168
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,000
he kills again.

169
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:15,920
This is too much.

170
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,720
You think you'll try it again?

171
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:23,140
If Fujinuma shows his face here,

172
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:24,980
I'm gonna take his ass out personally.

173
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,320
So what's the story with the high school girl?

174
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,720
She was in it with him.

175
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,960
Yeah, but he didn't want any loose threads,

176
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:33,420
so he tried to kill her too to shut her up.

177
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:35,500
Dragging her into the shit.

178
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:36,700
What an asshole.

179
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:38,940
They're wrong.

180
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,760
Please, Irie.

181
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:42,540
You don't have to apologize for anything.

182
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:43,600
Your uncle's right.

183
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,940
We didn't know there was a stalker after you.

184
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,000
You must have been so terrified.

185
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,940
But, Auntie, that's not...

186
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,040
You poor thing.

187
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,240
We shouldn't have left you all alone in the house like that.

188
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:54,980
You're wrong.

189
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,560
The police know who it is,

190
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,620
and they'll catch him soon.

191
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:59,660
You have nothing to worry about now.

192
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:01,180
They're all wrong.

193
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:15,120
Everyone thinks Satoru killed his mom and tried to kill me.

194
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,040
But that's crazy.

195
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,920
It doesn't matter what I say.

196
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:21,200
No one believes me.

197
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:31,260
You sure the message was sent from Sachko's phone?

198
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:31,900
Yeah.

199
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,240
Before I could get Irie out of the house,

200
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,940
she slipped her phone in my pocket.

201
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:37,520
Check it out.

202
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:41,100
You weren't kidding.

203
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,540
Looks like he wanted to help the cops catch you

204
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:45,220
by pinning the fire on you, too.

205
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,580
But why go to all that trouble?

206
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:50,100
I'm already a suspect in one murder.

207
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:51,080
Uh-uh.

208
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,940
This wasn't about framing me.

209
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,220
He was after Irie for another reason.

210
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:57,260
Do you think he tried to kill her

211
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,640
because she had something on him?

212
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:01,300
To get me to take the fall for my mom's murder,

213
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:03,300
he had to know when I'd be home to find her.

214
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:04,920
That means he knew my schedule.

215
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:08,220
So in the 24 hours between when my mom saw him

216
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:09,560
try to kidnap that little girl,

217
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:10,900
and when he killed my mom,

218
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:13,180
he must have gone to the pizza place

219
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:14,800
and had a look at the shift schedule.

220
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,540
If that's what happened,

221
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,280
I bet Irie saw his face.

222
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:20,980
He might even be someone I've seen before.

223
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,220
It's possible.

224
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:23,760
All we have to do is find out

225
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:25,300
who got behind the counter that day,

226
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,540
and we might have our killer.

227
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:28,440
Hell, it's worth a shot.

228
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,760
It might even break this case wide open.

229
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,480
I'm off to the hospital.

230
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:34,200
Uh, okay.

231
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,860
There's a report on the murders

232
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:37,780
from 18 years ago on my computer.

233
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:39,220
You should check it out.

234
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,700
I have a theory that Jun Shiratori

235
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:46,000
might suspect his father to be the killer.

236
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,500
Shiratori's refusal to talk to authorities

237
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,760
did not help his case.

238
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,720
Perhaps he did not want to say anything

239
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,520
that could possibly incriminate his father.

240
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:55,620
That figures.

241
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,080
Yuki loved his dad.

242
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:59,360
Kayo Hinazuki's classmates testified

243
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:02,280
they had seen her and Shiratori together many times.

244
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,820
The investigators focused on their testimonies

245
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:08,100
while ignoring Satoru Fujinuma's.

246
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:10,880
Suspects.

247
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,640
I don't know any of them besides Yuki and his dad.

248
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,540
They only had five?

249
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:19,380
The investigators thought Hiromi Sugita was murdered

250
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:21,560
because the killer mistook him for a girl.

251
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:23,640
Based on this assumption,

252
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:25,740
they made a list of five suspects,

253
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:27,720
none of whom knew Hiromi Sugita.

254
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,520
He eat today as folk dancing.

255
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,560
Ew, that sucks ass.

256
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:35,580
I don't want to hold some ugly girl's hand,

257
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:37,700
but I'd be okay holding Hiromi's.

258
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,660
Oh, that's butsy.

259
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,140
I think I know why Hiromi was murdered.

260
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,660
The killer knew he was a boy.

261
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,080
He only killed him to cover his tracks.

262
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,740
To keep his name off the list.

263
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:52,440
Jun Shiratori was arrested

264
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,700
after someone in the neighborhood

265
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:56,460
reported seeing him talking to a third grade girl.

266
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,640
The girl was alone at the time.

267
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,320
In the storage room of Shiratori Foods,

268
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:04,140
